        "by": "human",
        "reason": "Type B cast defect: TRY_TO_TIMESTAMP(REGEXP_REPLACE(col, offset-strip), \"yyyy-MM-dd'T'HH:mm:ss[.SSSSSS]\") returns NULL on any shape the pinned format misses (date-only values especially), and TRY_ makes it silent -- those NULLs reach the judge as differing_null_only/gap_shaped, i.e. a parse failure disguised as a FHIR coverage gap at the lower bar. Replace every datetime mapping with a bare TRY_CAST(col AS TIMESTAMP_NTZ). See pathling-sql SKILL.md and MIMIC_NOTES.md:337.",
        "superseded_decided_by": "judge",
        "superseded_justification": "MIMIC-on-FHIR provides no populated ICU input-event identifier at MedicationAdministration.identifier.value for relational inputevents.linkorderid. The ICU ETL, mimic-fhir/sql/fhir_medication_administration_icu.sql:7-23,38-103, never selects or writes linkorderid or any input-event identifier; its resource ID is an opaque UUIDv5 derived from stay_id-orderid-itemid, which neither contains nor permits recovery of linkorderid. This absence explains all 16,892 keyed differing_null_only rows: every candidate linkorderid is the required typed NULL while every representable value agrees. There are zero missing, invented, or conflicting rows. All defensible mappings were exhausted: exact medication system/code filtering, ICU Encounter identifier recovery, both effective-time variants, wall-time parsing, and dosage Quantity casting were implemented. Overall identity is 0.00% solely because linkorderid differs on every row; identity over representable columns is 100.00%. There are no divergent dependencies. The result remains a faithful port rather than a representation block because the complete row set and every representable column are reproduced exactly within comparator tolerances.",
        "superseded_status": "COMPLETED_WITH_DIVERGENCE"
      },
      {
